    <item>
      <title>Dmp Hunt4c2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/windows_rev/dmp_hunt4c2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/windows_rev/dmp_hunt4c2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;dmp-hunt4c2--net-memory-dump-analysis&#34;&gt;DMP Hunt4C2 — .NET Memory Dump Analysis&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#dmp-hunt4c2--net-memory-dump-analysis&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This walkthrough follows a .NET application from its call stack to its heap objects, then recovers an encrypted message from a Google Calendar event stored in memory.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The workflow:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Identify the .NET runtime&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  → Find application objects and crypto fields&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  → Recover the application assembly&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  → Decompile the message-handling code&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  → Read a Calendar event description from the heap&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  → Decrypt the recovered message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The addresses below come from this dump. For another dump, use the addresses returned by your own commands. Names such as &lt;code&gt;CRYPTO_OBJECT_ADDRESS&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;BASE_ADDRESS&lt;/code&gt; are placeholders to replace before running a command.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
